This is a collection of files used in the allHISQ project. The
directories for specific ensembles (except for
"l144288f211b700m000569m01555m1827") have not been updated for a long
time.

I just updated the "scripts" directory to the scripts I used on
Aurora.  I also added Aurora parameter files for
l144288f211b700m000569m01555m1827.

---------------------
Here are the allHISQ package requirements.

pyYAML and Cheetah

I haven't tried installing from github, but here are the locations:

https://github.com/cheetahtemplate/cheetah
https://github.com/yaml/pyyaml

To build, you need to set your PYTHONPATH to something like

$HOME/python_modules:$HOME/python_modules/lib/python

Then you can run (Note: these are old instructions.  Probably you can use python3 now.)

python2.7 ./setup.py install --prefix=$HOME/python_modules --install-lib=$HOME/python_modules/lib/python

for each of these packages.

--------------------------------------

MILC develop branch

ks_spectrum_hisq

Must be installed in the allHISQ/bin directory.

There have been some changes in the way the "coordinate_origin" and
"time_bc" are handled, so you need an up-to-date pull of this branch.


--------------------------------------

MILCprompts.py

Needs to be installed where Python finds installed packages.  I put
mine in ~/MILCprompts.py and added that path to $PYTHONPATH.
